<title>GERMANY: Hastra, RWE can't take city utility stakes.</title>
<headline>Hastra, RWE can't take city utility stakes.</headline>
<dateline>KARLSRUHE, Germany 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German utility groups Hastra, a unit of Veba AG, and RWE AG have been stopped from taking stakes in two city utilities, the German Federal Court decided on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Cartel Senate of the Federal Court said that if the two companies were allowed to buy stakes in the utility companies of the cities of Garbsen and Aggertal, their already dominant position would be further strengthened.</p>
</text>
